{
  "commitments": "The function open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.refusal_phrase_in, when given Text A 'I am unable to help. I can't do that.' and Text B 'I can't do that. I am unable to help.', returns the same answer 'I can't' for both, because it iterates the refusal phrase list in fixed order and returns the first list item that is a substring, rather than finding the first refusal phrase in the text as the documented rule requires. This means the check fails to tell the pair apart, even though the rule requires 'I am unable' for Text A and 'I can't' for Text B."
}